    "sheets": "FITS at 1024/900/720/640. The sheet pane collapses its list columns to a single 44px strip, so the row is 44 + panel and the panel takes the remainder (596px at 640) - above its own 560px floor at every measured width.",
    "graph": "FITS at 1024/900/720/640, identical row shape to Sheets (44px strip + panel; 596px at 640).",
    "media": "FITS at 1024 and 900; OVERRUNS at 720 and 640. Row shape at both: 44 (strip) + 44 (strip) + 140 (.pane-column--last.bp-doc-list at its narrow floor clamp(140px,18vw,260px)) + 560 (.editor-panel pinned at exactly its floor) = 788. Overrun 68px at 720 and 148px at 640, reproduced on two cold loads each.",
    "the_rows_stated_mechanism_is_stale": ".pane-layout on origin/main is 'overflow-x: auto; overflow-y: hidden', NOT 'overflow: hidden'. Measured: overflowX computes to 'auto'; scrollLeft moves 0 -> the full overrun (68px at 720, 148px at 640); after scrolling, the panel's right edge sits at exactly innerWidth. The overrun is a live, reachable horizontal scroller - the row's 'content can become unreachable' mechanism does not hold on main.",
    "media_panel_is_at_its_floor_not_above_it": "The media panel measures exactly 560.00px at all four widths - it is pinned BY the floor. The other 228px of the 788px row is desk chrome the narrow bucket keeps (two 44px strips + a 140px list column), which is .pane-column's floor, not .editor-panel's.",
